// =====================================================================================
//  Sister Groups & Member Transfer — one company, several independent groups
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  · Company: one Company Funds account (S.money), one fanbase of unique people (S.fb),
//    one member record per idol (S.members). Groups: S.groups (the first is the Main Group).
//  · Each group has its own production world. The ACTIVE group (S.ag) keeps its data in the
//    usual S fields, so every existing system (Single Production, songs & library, MV,
//    covers, albums, calendar, General Election…) works unchanged for that group. The other
//    groups keep theirs in g.ctx; switching groups swaps them (gsSwitch). Every day the
//    group-specific daily work also runs for every other group (gsDaily), so all groups
//    progress in parallel.
//  · Theater is per team / Trainee group already (S.th); each performance runs in its own
//    group's context, so venues, schedules, numbering and restrictions are independent.
//  · Concurrent Position (Kennin): m.kn = {gid,tid,from}; history in m.knh and m.mh.
//  · Transfer: permanent move to another group as Trainee or straight into a team.
//  · Member schedule: commitments of a member across groups; activities of DIFFERENT groups
//    that need the same member at overlapping times cannot both be confirmed.
//  · Finances: every ledger entry becomes a company transaction with its group (S.fin).
// =====================================================================================
